{"title":"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">2006 AMC 12A #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">2006 AMC 10A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Shortcut)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2  (Shortcut)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Cheap)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Cheap)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925501d29c6257d8f5714f6139ecbef82f132c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cut into two congruent hexagons, as shown, in such a way that the two hexagons can be repositioned without overlap to form a square.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66a524a2244d311dbe57cc4d9aaffc1b5e83bb03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=4; draw((0,4)--(18,4)--(18,-4)--(0,-4)--cycle); draw((6,4)--(6,0)--(12,0)--(12,-4)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,4),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(18,4),NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(18,-4),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,-4),SW); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(3,4),S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(15,-4),N); label(&quot;$18$&quot;,(9,4),N); label(&quot;$18$&quot;,(9,-4),S); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(0,0),W); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(18,0),E); dot((0,4)); dot((18,4)); dot((18,-4)); dot((0,-4));[/asy]\" width=\"295\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5eaded88bc7fc05e471d0c8b32561eb489d524b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 7\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 8\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 9\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hexagon\" title=\"Hexagon\">hexagons</a> are going to be repositioned to form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)\" title=\"Square (geometry)\"> square</a> without overlap, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> will remain the same. The rectangle's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee18ed2baf1e20b6f8eaa881b723506edb550b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18\\cdot8=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. This means the square will have four sides of length 12. The only way to do this is shown below.<br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/1794d4dcd643f680a8bcabca8f5ff34ed2b54a70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(175); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H; A=(0,8); B=(12,12); C=(12,4); D=(0,0); E=(0,12); F=(12,0); G=(6,4); H=(6,8); draw(A--E--B--C--G--H--A--D--F--C); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(12.6,4)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,E--B,N); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,D--F,S);  label(&quot;$4$&quot;,E--A,W); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(12.4,-1.75),E); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,A--D,W); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(12.4,4),E); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,A--H,S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,G--C,N); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"288\" />\n</p><p>As you can see from the diagram, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is half the length of the side of the square, which leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee619f9cece0d0453951a0da693e407e6a5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{12}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Shortcut.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Shortcut)\">Solution 2  (Shortcut)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2  (Shortcut)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As solution 1 says, the two hexagons are going to be repositioned to form a square without overlap. Thus we create this square out of the original rectangle.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc022e81e0d002b0a5b02d0aeef8906a0a7c4d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(175); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H; A=(0,8); B=(12,12); C=(12,4); D=(0,0); E=(0,12); F=(12,0); G=(6,4); H=(6,8); draw(A--E--B--C--G--H--A--D--F--C); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,A--H,S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,G--C,N); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"292\" />\n</p><p>As you can see from the diagram, the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> fits into the previously blank side, so we know that it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426d7ffa69ed286558677973799500f7f705626a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=4; draw((0,4)--(18,4)--(18,-4)--(0,-4)--cycle); draw((6,4)--(6,0)--(12,0)--(12,-4)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(9,-2),NW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,4),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(18,4),NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(18,-4),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,-4),SW); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(3,4),S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(15,-4),N); label(&quot;$18$&quot;,(9,4),N); label(&quot;$18$&quot;,(9,-4),S); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(0,0),W); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(18,0),E); dot((0,4)); dot((18,4)); dot((18,-4)); dot((0,-4));[/asy]\" width=\"295\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFrom there we can say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ceb55bf52a42744ba9527bcdd50ab0b438e42ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb625edfa95624ca8e91c44d48950d6ed426467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{18}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Ezraft\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Cheap.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Cheap)\">Solution 3 (Cheap)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Cheap)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the two hexagons are congruent, we know that the perpendicular line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is half of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Next, we plug the answer choices in to see which one works. Trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, we get the area of one hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> , as desired, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd68c07d997d2af0554e9141a1b121d95193e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> .\n</p><p>~coolmath2017\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A\">2006 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofprobl